      "page_title": "Write Buffers & Read-Side Backpressure",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Definition: The Write Buffer",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`transport.write()` **never** blocks; it always returns immediately",
            "Bytes the socket can't send yet queue in the ==write buffer==",
            "==high-water== mark: default **64 KiB**; ==low-water==: default high / 4",
            "Tune with `set_write_buffer_limits(high, low)`",
            "Inspect: `get_write_buffer_size()`, `get_write_buffer_limits()` → (low, high)"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "t.set_write_buffer_limits(",
            "    high=256*1024, low=64*1024)",
            "t.get_write_buffer_limits()",
            "# -> (65536, 262144)",
            "t.get_write_buffer_size()  # now"
          ],
          "note": "returns (low, high), not (high, low)"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Mechanism: Write Side"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              {
                "text": "fast producer",
                "ink": "black"
              },
              {
                "text": "write buffer",
                "sub": "grows",
                "ink": "blue"
              },
              {
                "text": "> high mark",
                "sub": "64 KiB",
                "ink": "red"
              },
              {
                "text": "pause_writing()",
                "ink": "red"
              },
              {
                "text": "drain",
                "sub": "socket sends",
                "ink": "blue"
              },
              {
                "text": "< low mark",
                "sub": "16 KiB",
                "ink": "green"
              },
              {
                "text": "resume_writing()",
                "ink": "green"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Condition",
            "Transport calls",
            "Protocol must"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "size > high",
              "`pause_writing()`",
              "**stop** producing"
            ],
            [
              "size < low",
              "`resume_writing()`",
              "produce again"
            ],
            [
              "ignores pause",
              "nothing more",
              "buffer → OOM"
            ]
          ],
          "highlightRow": 0,
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Mechanism: Read Side"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`pause_reading()`: socket leaves the selector, no more `data_received`",
            "`resume_reading()`: socket re-registered, callbacks restart",
            "Kernel receive buffer fills → ==TCP window== shrinks → sender slows",
            "That is **real** backpressure, reaching the remote peer",
            "`is_reading()` reports state; since 3.7 double pause/resume is a no-op"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Read API",
            "Effect"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`pause_reading()`",
              "off selector"
            ],
            [
              "`resume_reading()`",
              "back on selector"
            ],
            [
              "`is_reading()`",
              "True / False"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Why two marks?",
          "items": [
            "One threshold toggles on **every** item",
            "A ==gap== (e.g. 100 / 25) batches the switches",
            "Same idea as the 64 / 16 KiB write marks"
          ],
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Treat `pause_writing` as a hard **stop** signal",
            "Keep a ==gap== between high and low marks",
            "Always pair `pause_reading` with a resume path",
            "Prefer streams + `await drain()` unless you need raw speed"
          ],
          "style": "checkbox",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        }
      ],
      "hero": "python",
      "subtitle": "pause, drain, resume"
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Hysteresis & Obeying pause_writing",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Example: Hysteresis Pattern",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "def data_received(self, d):",
            "    self.q.append(d)",
            "    if len(self.q) > HIGH:  # 100",
            "        self.t.pause_reading()",
            "# consumer pops an item, then:",
            "if len(self.q) < LOW: resume()"
          ],
          "note": "LOW well below HIGH stops flapping"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Common Mistakes",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Ignoring `pause_writing` → write() buffers until memory runs out",
            "Expecting `write()` to block or raise when the buffer is full",
            "One threshold (LOW == HIGH) → pause/resume **flapping**",
            "Pausing reads with no resume path → connection stalls forever",
            "Streams handle this via `drain()` / 2×limit, covered on page 8"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "6. Example: Obeying pause_writing",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "class Sender(asyncio.Protocol):",
            "  def connection_made(self, t):",
            "    self.t = t",
            "    self.ok = asyncio.Event()",
            "    self.ok.set()",
            "  def pause_writing(self):",
            "    self.ok.clear()  # stop",
            "  def resume_writing(self):",
            "    self.ok.set()    # go again"
          ],
          "note": "producer awaits self.ok.wait() per chunk"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "7. Write vs Read Backpressure",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
