          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "try:",
            "  o, e = await asyncio.wait_for(",
            "      proc.communicate(), 10)",
            "except TimeoutError:",
            "  proc.kill()",
            "  await proc.wait()  # reap child"
          ],
          "note": "kill() alone leaves a zombie"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Common mistakes",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`await proc.wait()` with PIPE output **hangs** once output passes ~64 KiB",
            "Why: the child blocks writing to a full ==OS pipe buffer==",
            "Fix: `communicate()`, or read the pipes concurrently",
            "f-string into `create_subprocess_shell` without `shlex.quote` → injection",
            "`kill()` with no `await proc.wait()` → unreaped zombie"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "sticky",
          "title": "Rule of thumb",
          "text": "Use ==exec== by default. Use shell only for pipes and globs you wrote yourself. Always go through `communicate()` unless you are streaming."
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Graceful stop",
          "text": "Try `terminate()` first, `wait_for(proc.wait(), 5)`, and only then `kill()` + `await proc.wait()`."
        }
      ],
